# Apply theme UI via Docker

After **any** change under `wp-content/themes/sos-beauty/` (CSS, PHP, JS, assets):

1. Bump `SOS_BEAUTY_VERSION` in `functions.php` and `Version` in `style.css` (cache bust).
2. Run Docker apply (needs host Docker / OrbStack; use `required_permissions: ["all"]`):

```bash
cd /Users/nami/work/jp-hadang
docker compose up -d
docker compose restart wordpress
docker compose --profile cli run --rm --entrypoint wp wpcli --allow-root theme activate sos-beauty
docker compose --profile cli run --rm --entrypoint wp wpcli --allow-root cache flush
```

3. Verify `http://localhost:8080` responds (curl or browser). Tell user hard-refresh if browser still stale.

Do **not** skip this after UI work — bind-mount alone not enough when WP object/page cache or admin-ajax CDN-style headers linger.
